This extension adds Dying Light The Beast modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Auto-installs user's choice of Merger Utility.[/summary]

[size=2]This is not run automatically because it can take a minute, and it would be a nightmare when batch updating mods in Vortex.[/size]

[b][color=#ffff00][size=3]The extension will automatically download and install, based on user choice, either [color=#ffff00][size=3][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dyinglightthebeast/mods/699]Super Mod Merger[/url]﻿ (Recommended) or[/size][/color] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dyinglightthebeast/mods/140]UTM Mod Merger Utility[/url]. [/size][/color]
[size=3][b][color=#00ff00]You [u][i]MUST[/i][/u] run the merge tool after installing new mods for them to load. You will receive a notification to run the utility after deploying mods in Vortex. [/color][/b][/size][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]UTM Mod Merger Utility mods with a "unleashthemods.exe" file install to the "ph_ft" folder.[/*]
[*]Super Mod Merger mods with a "SuperModMerger.exe" file install to the "ph_ft" folder.[/*]
[*]Pak Mod (Merged) mods with a ".pak" file install to the "ph_ft\mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Root Folder mods with a "ph_ft" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Binaries (Engine Injector) mods install to the "ph_ft\work\bin\x64" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]UTM and Super Mod Merger are installed in the "ph_ft" folder and can be run from the Vortex Dashboard or the deployment notification.[/*]
[*][b][color=#ffff00]Users must run the Merger utility after deployment to load mods.[/color][/b][/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Dying Light The Beast mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Mergerutility:

Recognised when the archive contains a "unleashthemods.exe" file.

  Installs to: "ph_ft"

========================================================================

Supermerger:

Recognised when the archive contains a "SuperModMerger.exe" file.

  Installs to: "ph_ft"

========================================================================

Pak:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".pak" file.

  Installs to: "ph_ft\mods"

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── ph_ft\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "ph_ft" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Binaries:

Handled by the "testBinaries" installer. Inspect the extension source for the exact archive layout it expects.

  Installs to: "ph_ft\work\bin\x64"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives containing a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to the built-in FOMOD installer instead.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

